or  foxx's x-men films were in trouble  following the double disappointments of  x-men the last stand and x-men origins  wolverine but in true x-men fashion it  took a trip to the past to save their  future matthew vaughn's 2011 feature  x-men first class was a soft reboot for  the struggling series taking the team  back to the 1960s the era in which stan  lee and jack kirby created the comics in  the months before the cuban missile  crisis fassbender's eric lencher is a  metal manipulating nazi hunter and  charles xavier is a groovy telepath and  academic when the two men meet their  lives and the world are changed forever  mcavoy and fassbender lead the x-men  franchise into a new era and form the  emotional core of the four prequel  movies  the brutal dictatorship of ugandan  president idi amin is viewed through a  stranger's eyes in 2006's the last king  of scotland james mcavoy plays fictional  scottish doctor nicholas garrigan who  travels to uganda in the 1970s for  medical missionary work while there he  inadvertently charms his way into  becoming the personal physician and  confidant of the brutal and  unpredictable amine played by forrest  whitaker in his academy award-winning  performance director kevin mcdonald  brings his experience as a documentarian  into the last king of scotland giving it  a hazy discomforting sense of reality  whitaker is a towering presence and the  sydney morning herald commented on  mcavoy's turn as garrigan stating mcavoy  is dark and wiry and displays a nervy  egocentricity that is not particularly  likable does no damage to the film on  the contrary it helps to explain why he  should be so susceptible to a means  flattery  starter for 10 is an unquestionably  british coming-of-age story mcavoy is  brian a floppy-haired university student  in the 1980s who loves the television  quiz show university challenge while  trying to impress his university  challenge team brian's love triangle  with a flashy blonde and a feisty  brunette played by alice eve and rebecca  hall respectively may be too much of a  distraction this man has been sent from  the offices of university challenge  the film offers its fair share of 80s  nostalgia new order and kate bush are on  the soundtrack after all but mcavoy's  winning performance as a would-be trivia  champ gives starter pretend its vitality  prepare to be blindsided by how funny  this film is where else can you see  james mcavoy literally butt heads with  benedict cumberbatch and knock himself  out  the x-men film series arguably achieved  its greatest success with the 2014 time  traveling epic x-men days of future past  inspired by chris claremont and john  burns comic story of the same name which  has been continually ranked amongst the  best x-men storylines the film also saw  the return of director brian singer to  the franchise he departed after x2 x-men  united in the not-so-distant future  civilization is overrun by sentinels  advanced robots designed to hunt down  mutants the x-men have one last plan to  save the world send wolverine's mind  back in time to his younger body once  he's there he can reunite mcavoy's  professor x and fassbender's magneto and  stop jennifer lawrence's mystique from  committing the assassination that will  launch the sentinels x-men days of  future past combines mutants machines  and the plots of a 70s political  thriller to produce one of the best  films in the superhero genre amid the  star-studded cast featuring original  x-men cast members and new faces there  is one standout performance that  completely reinvents a role the  atlantic's review put it best writing  mcavoy is the real star of the show  put aside the time travel giant robots  and muted angst x-men days of future  past is the story of one man learning to  hope again check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite movies and  stars are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

